12. What happens when we concatenate Strings?

When we concatenate Strings, Java creates a new String containing the combined content because String objects are immutable. The original Strings are not modified.

*****************Example:
String s1 = "Hello";
String s2 = "Java";

String s3 = s1 + " " + s2;

System.out.println(s3);

Output:

Hello Java

